  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Sunday) \nIssued at 913 AM CDT Sun Oct 11 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge will gradually break down during the long\nterm forecast period bringing another taste of Fall-like weather\nby this weekend. Warm conditions will continue on Thursday as we\nonce again see temperatures rise into the upper 80s to lower 90s.\nOn Friday, a low pressure system drops down from Canada into the \nGreat Lakes region with a cold front positioned to its south. Due\nto the lack of moisture associated with this front, no precip is\nexpected as it passes through the local forecast area on Friday.\nHowever, an airmass change begins to occur with NW flow advecting\nin much cooler and drier conditions. We will start to feel this\nchange Friday night as temperatures are forecast to drop into the\nupper 40s to lower 50s. This upcoming weekend will truly feel \nlike Fall as temperatures warm only into the upper 60s to lower \n70s with overnight lows in the low to mid 40s.",
